PATCH 338: FUN_0000_a18e -- the point-struct projection trampoline (asm 0xa18e: `call 0x578; retf`)
truncated its two POINT-STRUCT POINTER params to 16 bits.  a18e's param_4/param_5 were typed undefined2
(uint16_t), so when addb (patch 337) calls a18e(param_1,param_2,param_3, obj+4, &DAT_2000_5690) the two
HOST pointers get truncated to their low 16 bits; a18e forwards them to 0578 -> 0731, which dereferences
`*param_1`/`*param_2` -> SIGSEGV at the truncated near-address (fault ~0xfcac on the
b5e7->addb->a18e->0578->0731 flight-tick chain).  Same class as patch 328/330 (undefined2 point-struct
pointer truncation).

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0xa18e; DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00): a18e is a pure
`call 0x578; retf` forwarder; 0578 already types param_4/param_5 `int` and 0731 takes `uint*`.  All three
a18e call sites (fist.c 59919/60855/60903 + addb) pass HOST pointers (&DAT_2000_568x/569x, param_3+4,
obj+4) as param_4/param_5.  The only truncation is a18e's undefined2 param typing.

FIX: widen a18e's param_4/param_5 (both the forward decl and the definition) to `int` (matching 0578's
int params), so the 32-bit host pointer passes through intact.  Behaviour-neutral for the 24 verify flows
(mission-cascade only).
